{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>He began with the eldest.</b> So that they would not sense that he knew the goblet was only in Benjamin's sack; and he did this in order to act as a stranger to them." "<b>And the goblet was found in Benjamin's sack.</b> They would shame him and call him 'thief, son of a thiefess,' because it is written (Genesis 31:19) ״ותגנוב רחל את התרפים״, and they would strike him on his shoulders. And because they suspected him though there was no sin in him, the Shekhinah dwelt in his portion; this is why it is written (Deuteronomy 33:12–13) ״ובין כתפיו שכן״. And what is written, ״ויקרעו שמלותם״ — Benjamin too is included; and because they suspected him though he was blameless, he was rewarded and received a crown for this, in that there went forth from him Mordecai, who tore his garments over Israel, as it says, ״ויקרע מרדכי את בגדיו״. But they were worthy of this, for on account of their grandmother their father tore his garments, as it says (Genesis 37:34) ״ויקרע יעקב שמלותיו״ — and so the matter is measure for measure, whether for punishment or for reward. And that the brothers of Joseph tore their garments, all of it was through Menasheh, for what is written ״ויצו את אשר על ביתו״ — it was Menasheh; and because he did all this affair and was the agent to pursue after them and to toy with them over the goblet, and was the cause that they tore their garments, therefore his inheritance was torn — half in the land of Canaan and half across the Jordan."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {1 "Rabbeinu Bahya reads ובין כתפיו שכן (Deut. 33:12, the blessing of Benjamin) as a direct response to the brothers striking Benjamin on his shoulders; the verse citation range includes the next verse (33:13) in the Hebrew, perhaps because the printed text groups the continuation of Benjamin's blessing."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:15.451840741Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}